course: dictionary
lesson: 5379
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A knife is a tool with a sharp blade and a handle, used for cutting. «Walk, never run, in the kitchen: knives, hot pans and slippery floors make running dangerous.» Here knives is the plural, so it means more than one knife.
explain: Knife can also be a piece of table cutlery, used for eating. «When a table is laid, every person gets a knife, a fork and a spoon.» Knife and fork always go together at the table.
explain: Context tells you which meaning a word has. A knife in the drawer is a tool. To knife someone means to attack them with a knife, which is rare and very serious. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: Phrases use knife in special ways. «Not the sharpest knife in the drawer» is a joke that means someone is not very clever. «On a knife edge» means a situation that is very uncertain.
fact: A knife is a tool with a sharp blade and a handle, used for cutting.
fact: Knives is the plural of knife: one knife, two knives.
fact: At the table, the knife goes on the right, and you use it with a fork.
fact: In the kitchen, carry a knife with the point down, and never try to catch a falling knife.
fact: «Not the sharpest knife in the drawer» means someone is not very clever; it is a humorous phrase.
exercise: «Walk, never run, in the kitchen: knives, hot pans and slippery floors make running dangerous.» Find and copy the plural of knife. | kitchen | *knives | slippery | running
exercise: «When a table is laid, every person gets a knife, a fork and a spoon.» What is a knife in this sentence? | *A piece of cutlery for eating | A tool for chopping wood | A sharp kind of spoon | A type of drawer
exercise: What is the safest way to carry a knife in the kitchen? | Running across the room with it | Tossing it to a friend | With the point up, waving it about | *With the point down, close to your side
test: What does «not the sharpest knife in the drawer» mean? | A drawer that is very tidy | Someone who is very sharp and quick | A knife that needs sharpening | *Someone who is not very clever
test: When a table is laid, where does the knife go? | In the middle of the table | *On the right | On the left | Under the plate
exam: Which sentence uses knife to mean a piece of cutlery? | A knife has a sharp blade and a handle | Taking a knife to school is against the rules | *Every person gets a knife, a fork and a spoon when the table is laid | To knife someone is a serious attack
